# state: returning   (written from sonic-heroes.returning-observe-20261001T171059, slot 01 present; lane.savestate433)
# Sonic Heroes (5345002B). CONFIRMED on the Nova (session 58, 2026-10-01,
# scratch/judge/sonic-heroes-171639): one full unattended `route.sh` replay
# ran every scripted step through `mark gameplay` (172133, Seaside Hill,
# HUD live) and three `play` shots after it (172141/172150/172201) show the
# score (60->80), ring count (006->008) and timer all advancing and Sonic
# changing pose/position between frames -- live, evolving play, not a
# stuck menu or cutscene. Replaces the session 46 9-cycle START/A route that
# two Thor re-screens showed was a coin flip: session 47's run landed in
# live play, session 48's identical run landed on a frozen PAUSE menu (a
# START press during live play, with no un-pause step after it). A fixed
# cycle count races the title's own variable boot/cutscene length and does
# not reliably land clear of a live level.
#
# This route is driven from per-step nav.py observation on the Nova
# (nav/sonic-heroes.observe-20261001T170546 on a disk with NO game data, and
# nav/sonic-heroes.returning-observe-20261001T171059 on the disk this first
# session left behind, WITH game data in slot 01), not guessed cycle counts:
#   - fresh disk: title -> START -> "no Game Data... Create Game Data 01?"
#     (Create highlighted, A) -> "Game Data has been created... press A" (A)
#     -> Main Menu.
#   - disk with slot 01 present: title -> START -> slot grid (No.01
#     highlighted, A) -> Start/Delete/Cancel (Start highlighted, A) -> Main
#     Menu.
#   Both paths reach Main Menu after exactly ONE START and THREE A presses,
#   with the default option already highlighted at every screen, so one
#   route covers both disk states (the dispatch run starts from whatever
#   the disk holds, not from nav state -- see NOTES.md session 57's
#   ADDENDUM-7 Castlevania lesson).
# From Main Menu: A (1P PLAY, default) -> A (STORY, default) -> A (TEAM
# SONIC, default) -> an ~85-90 s in-engine cutscene/dialogue with NO input
# (both nav sessions: 88 s and 85 s to live play) -> Seaside Hill, Team
# Sonic running, full HUD, timer counting. No STARTs after the title's: the
# only in-level pause trap is a START while already in play, and this route
# never presses one again.
# Confirmed by nav.py movement tests in both sessions: a left-stick press
# changed Sonic's screen position and the camera panned off the cutscene's
# fixed framing (not true of a stuck cutscene frame).
wait 30
shot boot30
wait 30
shot boot60
wait 30
shot boot90
wait 20
shot boot110
wait 15
shot pretitle
mark booted
press START
wait 8
shot menu1
press A
wait 8
shot menu2
press A
wait 10
shot menu3
press A
wait 6
shot story
press A
wait 6
shot team
press A
wait 8
shot cutscene-start
wait 100
shot cutscene-end
# ADDENDUM 10 (owner, 2026-10-01 ~18:35 PDT): the owner played this on the
# Nova and found the prior loop's 1.5 s LX min/max swings made Sonic wander
# rather than advance ("We should be holding down 'up' so it advances").
# Hold LY min (stick UP) continuously for the rest of the route -- no LX
# swings, no returning to mid -- and press A only occasionally for a jump.
# Never press START again (the in-level pause trap this route already
# avoids). `shot play` every ~10 s so a frame review can see Sonic's
# position and the HUD advance between shots.
mark gameplay
axis LY min
repeat forever {
    wait 10
    shot play
    wait 10
    shot play
    wait 10
    press A
    shot play
}
